	"kit": "quaternius_scifi",
	"source": "Quaternius Modular Sci-Fi MegaKit, Standard tier (CC0). Measured with tools/inventory_kit.gd.",
	"notes": [
		"Kit grid is 4 m and walls are 3.0 m, so the kit-wide scale is 0.75 across and 1.0 up: a wall piece becomes 2 tiles (3.0 m) long and stays 3.0 m tall.",
		"A piece's transform is scale, then pitch (degrees, about +X), then yaw (degrees, about +Y), then offset (metres, socket space). At rotation 0 its room side faces +Z and its origin is on the socket.",
		"wall_light pieces are the kit's ceiling light panels stood up on a wall: pitch -90 turns their lit underside (-Y) to face the room (+Z), and offset x centres them on the socket, which MapBuilder puts on the wall face at lamp height. width is the panel's length along the wall, so a doorway lamp can pick one that clears the door frame.",
		"Kit walls sit on the x = -2 edge of their 4 m tile with the room on +X, hence yaw -90 and offset z 1.5 (the scaled 2 m half-tile).",
		"tiles is a wall piece's length along its run. squash marks the pieces that may be squeezed to 50% to fill a 1-tile run.",
		"opening is a door frame's clear width and top in kit metres, and outer_width its full width: MapBuilder scales a frame across so the opening spans the DOOR run.",
		"per_cell places that many copies in a 2x2 grid inside each footprint cell.",
		"Left out after screenshots: Platform_Metal2, Platform_3Plates and Platform_CenterPlate read as flat grey squares at one tile; WallWindow_Straight's glass imports opaque white; WallAstra_Straight_Flat reads as bare white slabs beside the banded walls; Door_Frame_Square clears only 2.10 m at 0.6 height.",
		"The mk_* pieces are placeholder furniture for ROOM_ASSETS_SOURCING.md and follow the furniture convention in kaykit_furniture.json's notes: origin at the footprint centre on the floor, long side along X, front +Z; footprint in tiles; tier light, heavy, dressing, clutter, wall or door. Their sockets wait for ROOM_THEMES_PLAN.md D.1 and D.6."
	],
